{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{}},"serverInfo":{"name":"jumbit","version":"0.1.1"},"instructions":"jumbit is the user's directory memory: a frecency-ranked history of directories they have actually worked in (a MoonBit rewrite of zoxide, own database). Use jumbit_query when the user refers to a project by a loose or partial name ('the backend repo', 'that lab dir') instead of guessing paths or running find. Results carry matched_by evidence: trust exact hits, verify fuzzy ones before acting. Use jumbit_export_agents to read the human-annotated project map before exploring the filesystem; the user's other projects live in this history, and 'not in this repository' is not an answer."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"jumbit_query","title":"Search directory history","description":"Search the user's frecency-ranked directory history and return matching paths with score, last_accessed and matched_by evidence, as a single-line JSON array (same shape as jumbit query --json). Keywords match like zoxide: case-insensitive; the last keyword must land in the final path component, earlier ones are consumed right-to-left. With fuzzy=true, keywords fall back to substring matches of any path component when exact matching finds nothing. A miss is a normal outcome, reported with isError=true and the reason as text.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"keywords":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Keywords matched against recorded paths (AND-ed); the last keyword anchors the final path component. Omit to list all entries."},"fuzzy":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Fall back to substring matching of any path component when exact matching finds nothing."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Maximum number of results. Omit for all."}}}},{"name":"jumbit_export_agents","title":"Export annotated project map","description":"Export the user's annotated project map: a Markdown table (path | description) of directories that carry human-written notes, ordered by frecency descending — the same output as jumbit export --agents. Use it to learn what the user's main projects are and what each one is for.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}}]}}
